      "problem": "If the equation ${log}_{1/4}⁡64=-3$ is equivalent to ${b}^{-3}=a,$  then $a=${{field-1}}.",
      "worked_solution": "The logarithm of $a$ with base $b$ is defined as follows:\n\n${log}_{b}⁡a=x$ is equivalent to $a={b}^{x}$\n\nIf we compare ${log}_{1/4}⁡64=-3$ with ${log}_{b}⁡a=x,$ we get $a=64,$ $b=\\frac{1}{4},$ and $x=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the equation ${log}_{1/4}⁡64=-3$ is equivalent to ${(\\frac{1}{4})}^{-3}=64.$ Consequently, $a=64.$",
